In a couple of topics in the past
[http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/f3a5d94843fb37f3/b3fec0fccac83de8?q=wearing+a+bag&rnum=1#b3fec0fccac83de8]
it's been suggested that one should be able to wear a bag on one's
head. So, here's a patch.

You can now wear a bag over your head using the 'P'ut command.

Bags take up the eye slot, so you can't wear towels, lenses or
blindfolds with them.

Wearing a non-magical bag causes its contents to fall out (bags of
holding hold onto their items.)

You can't wear a bag of holding if it is heavier than 2 dwarvish iron
helms. (i.e 100 units.)

You can't use bags while wearing them.

Trying to wear a bag of tricks causes the bag to "empty a gallon of
whitewash onto you" which rusts your helmet and abuses wisdom.

Wearing a bag brings these benefits:
* You are completely immune to mind flayer tentacle attacks.
* Your helmet is completely immune to enemy rust attacks.
* Your helmet can't be stolen.
* Your helmet may be protected from rust.
* Your helmet is protected from burning.

NOTE: Cursed bags of holding won't "cause your head to disappear" for
two reasons. One, you can't remove the bag from your head if it's
cursed. Two, bags of holding can only vanish items if they are
completely contained in the bag.

A link to the patch is at http://www.greyfire.org/~l/ - along with a
few more patches I wrote.

I'm fairly certain that the patch itself is bug-free... ...but by
virtue of saying it out loud I've just doomed myself and everyone who
trusts me. Well, enjoy!



